**Prompt:** write a script that will generate glowing text with a rainbow color animated gradient border around the glowing text. using CSS and HTML

---

**My Answer:**

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <title>Glowing Rainbow Text with Animated Border</title>
  <style>
    body {
      background: #111;
      min-height: 100vh;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: center;
      margin: 0;
    }
    .rainbow-border {
      padding: 16px 32px;
      border-radius: 16px;
      position: relative;
      background: linear-gradient(90deg, red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo, violet, red);
      background-size: 400% 400%;
      animation: rainbow 6s linear infinite;
      /* To create a border effect, use a pseudo-element or inner box */
      display: inline-block;
    }
    .rainbow-border .glow-text {
      background: #111;
      border-radius: 12px;
      padding: 16px 32px;
      color: #fff;
      font-size: 2.5rem;
      font-weight: bold;
      text-align: center;
      text-shadow:
        0 0 8px #fff,
        0 0 16px #fff,
        0 0 32px #ff00de,
        0 0 48px #ff00de;
      position: relative;
      z-index: 1;
      display: block;
    }
    /* Optional: Use a pseudo-element for a more "border" look */
    .rainbow-border::before {
      content: "";
      position: absolute;
      inset: 0;
      border-radius: 16px;
      padding: 4px;
      background: inherit;
      z-index: 0;
      filter: blur(4px);
      opacity: 0.7;
    }
    @keyframes rainbow {
      0% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
      50% { background-position: 100% 50%; }
      100% { background-position: 0% 50%; }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div class="rainbow-border">
    <span class="glow-text">Glowing Rainbow Text</span>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

