Given your scenario—multiple account types (DoctorAccount, UserAccount, and potentially more in the future), each with its own repository, and a service layer that retrieves an account by id and type—the best design pattern is the **Strategy Pattern** combined with a **Factory or Registry**. This allows you to encapsulate the retrieval logic for each account type and easily extend the system for new types without modifying existing code, adhering to the Open/Closed Principle.

**Implementation Outline:**

1. **Define a common interface for account retrieval:**

```java
public interface AccountRetrievalStrategy {
    Object findById(Integer id);
    boolean supports(String accountType);
}
```

2. **Implement the interface for each account type:**

```java
@Service
public class DoctorAccountRetrievalStrategy implements AccountRetrievalStrategy {
    @Autowired
    private DoctorAccountRepository doctorAccountRepository;

    @Override
    public Object findById(Integer id) {
        return doctorAccountRepository.findById(id).orElse(null);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean supports(String accountType) {
        return "doctor".equalsIgnoreCase(accountType);
    }
}

@Service
public class UserAccountRetrievalStrategy implements AccountRetrievalStrategy {
    @Autowired
    private UserAccountRepository userAccountRepository;

    @Override
    public Object findById(Integer id) {
        return userAccountRepository.findById(id).orElse(null);
    }

    @Override
    public boolean supports(String accountType) {
        return "user".equalsIgnoreCase(accountType);
    }
}
```

3. **Create a factory or registry to select the correct strategy:**

```java
@Component
public class AccountStrategyFactory {
    private final List<AccountRetrievalStrategy> strategies;

    @Autowired
    public AccountStrategyFactory(List<AccountRetrievalStrategy> strategies) {
        this.strategies = strategies;
    }

    public AccountRetrievalStrategy getStrategy(String accountType) {
        return strategies.stream()
            .filter(s -> s.supports(accountType))
            .findFirst()
            .orElseThrow(() -> new IllegalArgumentException("Unsupported account type: " + accountType));
    }
}
```

4. **Service layer usage:**

```java
@Service
public class AccountService {
    @Autowired
    private AccountStrategyFactory factory;

    public Object getAccountById(String accountType, Integer id) {
        return factory.getStrategy(accountType).findById(id);
    }
}
```

