### 1. Multiple SecurityFilterChain Beans with RequestMatcher

Since Spring Security 5, you can define multiple `SecurityFilterChain` beans, each with its own `RequestMatcher`. For header-based matching, you can use `RequestHeaderRequestMatcher` or implement a custom `RequestMatcher` for more complex logic.

**Example:**

```java
@Bean
public SecurityFilterChain refererAFilterChain(HttpSecurity http) throws Exception {
    http
        .requestMatcher(new RequestHeaderRequestMatcher("Referer", "https://refererA.com"))
        .addFilterBefore(new FilterForRefererA(), UsernamePasswordAuthenticationFilter.class)
        .authorizeRequests().anyRequest().authenticated();
    return http.build();
}

