Your current Trie implementation uses a `vector<Node*>` of size 26 for each node, which is not memory efficient because each node allocates a vector object (with its own metadata and heap allocation) even though the size is always fixed. Here are some ways to make your code more memory efficient:

1. **Use a fixed-size array instead of vector:**  
   Since the number of children is always 26 (for lowercase English letters), you can use a plain C-style array or `std::array<Node*, 26>`. This avoids the overhead of the vector object and its dynamic allocation.

   ```cpp
